From ead069dd57ddcb9001f53163068dc7fa90623baa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:12:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron): defer due jobs under the core-update drain hold;
 cut cron runs in an update restart past hermes-sync's cron bound [daveey]

hermes-hub 2026-10-30 16:19-16:53 UTC: cron runs that started while hermes-sync's drain held new
kanban claims kept the drain busy; the update applied after 34.1 min against a 30 min target
(t_01a18dbde9f8b2f0).

- cron tick honours <home>/core-update/drain-hold (the signal the kanban dispatcher reads): due
  jobs stay due, each is named once per hold, recurring jobs catch up once after the hold and
  one-shots are covered by the planned pause. A dead drainer's hold does not count.
- restart wait: an update intent marked "cron_cut": true puts awaitable cron runs under the
  15 s core-update cap, logging each cut run (job id, start time). A chat turn keeps its wait.
---
